WEBVTT

00:47.005 --> 00:48.423
Oh, start?

00:48.506 --> 00:49.466
MAY, 2011

00:49.549 --> 00:50.550
Uh…

00:51.134 --> 00:52.802
Hey. Hello. How are you?

00:56.347 --> 00:58.349
My name is Choi Ung.

00:58.433 --> 00:59.934
CHOI UNG (19, MALE)

01:00.018 --> 01:01.394
Let's look at the first one.

01:01.478 --> 01:04.731
As you can see,
value x is approaching one,

01:04.814 --> 01:07.358
there's a limiting value of function x.

01:07.442 --> 01:09.736
In this case, we need to think
of how to get the value

01:09.819 --> 01:11.321
when it's smaller than one.

01:11.404 --> 01:13.907
I'll also show you what to do
when it's bigger than one.

01:13.990 --> 01:15.909
But so far, do you understand?

01:15.992 --> 01:18.286
Don't look at the camera.

01:18.369 --> 01:19.579
It's too big for me to miss.

01:19.662 --> 01:22.248
Just pretend like
there's nothing over here.

01:22.332 --> 01:24.000
How am I supposed to do that?
It's right in front of me.

01:24.084 --> 01:26.336
Ignore it.

01:27.170 --> 01:29.297
As you can see, well…

01:30.006 --> 01:31.382
those guys are filming me.

01:31.466 --> 01:33.593
Hey, you idiot. Face forward.

01:33.676 --> 01:35.512
Now, look at the next one.

01:36.596 --> 01:38.473
But it's not just me.

01:38.556 --> 01:41.643
Why are you looking at me?
Look at the chalkboard.

01:42.769 --> 01:46.231
Using this formula, you can see
the limiting values are actually the same.

01:47.524 --> 01:49.192
This annoying girl is part
of it too.

01:49.275 --> 01:50.401
We're done.

01:51.861 --> 01:54.280
Everyone, please bow to our teacher.

01:54.364 --> 01:55.824
Thank you, ma'am.

01:57.242 --> 01:58.743
You're leaving?

01:58.827 --> 02:00.870
None of your business.
Why should I tell you?

02:06.501 --> 02:09.254
Excuse me, sir,
can I stop recording for a moment?

02:09.337 --> 02:11.548
It's really hard
to work with such an idiot.

02:11.631 --> 02:12.549
Keep rolling.

02:12.632 --> 02:14.634
- You call me an idiot?
- We've been filming for days.

02:14.717 --> 02:16.594
And the whole time, you kept
moving around like you're crazy.

02:16.678 --> 02:19.222
I couldn't focus at all
because you were so restless.

02:19.806 --> 02:22.100
The camera was right there.
What the heck do you want me to do?

02:22.183 --> 02:24.811
You just gotta focus in class.
Are you saying can't you do that?

02:24.894 --> 02:26.771
Why don't you ignore me
and focus all by yourself?

02:26.855 --> 02:28.231
Are you saying you can't do that?

02:28.314 --> 02:30.942
All right, I guess you don't care at all
about getting good grades.

02:31.025 --> 02:32.443
Sure, I totally get it.

02:32.527 --> 02:34.988
But still, I refuse
to let you drag me down with you.

02:37.282 --> 02:38.950
You heard everything, right?

02:39.033 --> 02:41.536
I'm so happy for you.
Your social skills can't get lower.

02:43.413 --> 02:44.789
Why did I agree to this?

02:44.873 --> 02:47.625
Yeah, I know, right?
Why did you agree to do this?

02:50.211 --> 02:51.546
My name is Kook Yeon-su.

02:51.629 --> 02:52.589
KOOK YEON-SU (19, FEMALE)

02:53.214 --> 02:56.050
I think I first saw Choi Ung
in the tenth grade.

02:57.427 --> 02:59.554
Wow, you're borrowing so many again?

02:59.637 --> 03:01.848
I'm reading less
because I have exams soon.

03:01.931 --> 03:05.059
By the time you graduate,
you'll have read all the books.

03:05.643 --> 03:07.520
Kook Yeon-su…

03:07.604 --> 03:10.607
- Here. Enjoy reading.
- Thank you very much.

03:14.694 --> 03:16.529
APRIL'S TOP BOOKWORMS

03:16.613 --> 03:18.156
1ST: CHOI UNG
2ND: KOOK YEON-SU

03:20.491 --> 03:22.202
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

03:22.285 --> 03:23.745
Who is this Choi Ung?

03:23.828 --> 03:25.496
He's first place this month too?

03:25.580 --> 03:27.290
Oh, right, Ung?

03:28.041 --> 03:29.667
He's sitting right over there.

03:34.422 --> 03:35.590
Hey.

03:36.549 --> 03:39.052
I met him
in the most unlikely place.

03:39.135 --> 03:40.511
My name is Kook Yeon-su.

03:40.595 --> 03:42.388
Tell me, what's your rank?

03:42.472 --> 03:44.682
- My what?
- Your standing in school.

03:45.725 --> 03:47.644
I'm 267.

03:48.478 --> 03:50.563
But we only have…

03:50.647 --> 03:52.774
267 students.

03:53.483 --> 03:57.237
In that moment,
I thought he was a really strange kid.

04:01.449 --> 04:03.117
Oh, wait, hang on.

04:03.201 --> 04:05.036
That was the second time we met.

04:05.119 --> 04:07.455
The first time was
during the entrance ceremony.

04:07.538 --> 04:10.667
The student who entered
at the top of the year is Kook Yeon-su.

04:10.750 --> 04:13.002
Congratulations.

04:14.420 --> 04:17.131
Her name's Kook Yeon-su?
No wonder the girl's smart.

04:17.215 --> 04:19.467
I watched her
because the way she walked

04:19.550 --> 04:21.761
was like she was marching
onto a battlefield.

04:25.431 --> 04:27.809
HWIYEONG HIGH SCHOOL
ENTRANCE CEREMONY

04:28.851 --> 04:30.687
Hey, look at her skirt.

04:30.770 --> 04:32.647
She's obviously a teacher's pet.

04:32.730 --> 04:36.150
They have the same style. I gotta say,
I'm not surprised she got that award.

04:36.234 --> 04:39.320
Look at her shoes. Even my mom
wouldn't be caught dead wearing that.

04:40.238 --> 04:42.031
I know, so tacky, right?

04:42.115 --> 04:44.784
…schoolers.
I would like to thank you all for being…

04:44.867 --> 04:47.996
To be clear, I was trying to be nice
to her the first time our eyes met.

04:48.079 --> 04:49.747
Hey.

04:50.248 --> 04:51.499
Turn around.

04:53.293 --> 04:56.546
That's when I realized
she was pretty weird.

05:05.305 --> 05:06.848
Anyway, I never imagined

05:06.931 --> 05:09.267
that I would get involved
with a kid as strange as him.

05:10.268 --> 05:11.602
Oh, good, you're here.

05:11.686 --> 05:13.438
Did you think about that offer
I was telling you?

05:13.521 --> 05:15.315
The producer of the show's
a good friend of mine.

05:15.398 --> 05:16.816
And he promised
he wouldn't get in your way.

05:16.899 --> 05:19.694
But if you think it'll affect
your studies, you can refuse.

05:19.777 --> 05:22.280
- Am I the only one you're going to film?
- No, there's another.

05:22.363 --> 05:24.907
They'll observe the best student
and the worst student for a month,

05:24.991 --> 05:26.326
to see how they'll spend time together.

05:26.409 --> 05:27.660
Kind of like a documentary.

05:29.412 --> 05:30.955
Anyway, just think about it.

05:35.793 --> 05:40.048
Well, let's say I agree to it.
Are they going to pay me or something?

05:40.131 --> 05:41.632
Of course. You'll be paid.

05:47.388 --> 05:50.808
To me, it looked like
he was my complete opposite.

05:52.518 --> 05:54.812
Oh, my goodness, you're here.

05:54.896 --> 05:58.191
Oh. Hang on. Just a moment.
I'll be right back. Yes, hold on.

05:59.275 --> 06:00.943
Oh, the ingredients are here.

06:01.027 --> 06:02.320
Please, check them thoroughly.

06:02.403 --> 06:04.822
Yeah, because last time,
they weren't really the best.

06:04.906 --> 06:07.075
So check it real well, okay.
I'll be off now, see you.

06:07.158 --> 06:10.828
SEAFOOD SOUP WITH UNG
POTATO SOUP WITH UNG

06:10.912 --> 06:12.580
CHICKEN FEET WITH UNG

06:12.663 --> 06:14.999
- I see him, there he is.
- Hello.

06:15.083 --> 06:17.418
Finally, he's here. This is Ung's father.

06:18.127 --> 06:19.712
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Hello.

06:20.755 --> 06:22.131
- Ung!
- Oh, hey, son!

06:22.215 --> 06:23.591
- Come over here. Sit down.
- Turns out…

06:23.674 --> 06:25.968
events will unfold
regardless of my intentions.

06:26.052 --> 06:28.054
Start talking. Why didn't you
mention the documentary?

06:28.137 --> 06:30.014
Why would I? I said I'm not gonna do it.

06:30.098 --> 06:32.809
What are you talking about? The producer
came all the way here for you.

06:32.892 --> 06:34.644
- You shouldn't miss this chance.
- That's true.

06:34.727 --> 06:36.479
You'll be studying
with the top student of the year.

06:36.562 --> 06:38.648
- Of course you should do the show.
- Of course!

06:38.731 --> 06:41.984
Another thing. We have no idea
what our boy does at school the whole day.

06:42.068 --> 06:45.238
If you film him, will we be able
to see what sort of activities he does?

06:45.321 --> 06:47.407
- Of course.
- Oh, thank you, sir. Thank you.

06:47.490 --> 06:48.658
But I really don't want to!

06:48.741 --> 06:50.201
Why the hell not? How could you refuse?

06:50.284 --> 06:53.704
I don't want to,
because strangers will know my face.

06:53.788 --> 06:55.706
But think of the unforgettable memories
you'll be making.

06:55.790 --> 06:57.667
- Right.
- I'm a senior now, you know.

06:57.750 --> 07:00.753
Don't you think doing this thing
will affect my academics?

07:01.879 --> 07:03.131
Is he kidding?

07:03.214 --> 07:06.134
Did you forget you'll be studying
with the top student of your year?

07:06.217 --> 07:07.760
You should be grateful for this chance!

07:07.844 --> 07:08.761
I mean…

07:08.845 --> 07:11.681
It was as if
things had to happen that way.

07:11.764 --> 07:13.766
That girl is such a weirdo!

07:14.392 --> 07:17.645
And that's it,
that's how this whole thing started.

07:22.817 --> 07:24.277
Now, everyone, please pay attention.

07:24.360 --> 07:27.155
Choi Ung from Class 1
will join us for a month.

07:27.238 --> 07:28.573
Yes, sir.

07:28.656 --> 07:30.324
I want you all
to be nice to him.

07:30.408 --> 07:32.285
It may be distracting for you
since they'll be filming,

07:32.368 --> 07:34.328
but it'll be a fun experience.

07:34.412 --> 07:36.873
Make sure you cooperate
with them at all times.

07:36.956 --> 07:39.000
If none of you have any more concerns,
I'll go now.

07:39.083 --> 07:40.877
Bye, sir.

08:04.150 --> 08:06.444
It was more bothersome
than I thought.

08:18.456 --> 08:21.167
It's the worst students
to make the most fuss.

08:22.502 --> 08:25.463
- Are you talking to me?
- Keep your stuff off my desk or else.

08:35.473 --> 08:37.517
She was more annoying.

08:37.600 --> 08:39.685
Way more than I had imagined.

08:46.317 --> 08:49.195
At first, I tried
real hard to be friends with her.

08:49.278 --> 08:50.404
Hey…

09:05.294 --> 09:06.254
Sorry.

09:19.767 --> 09:21.060
I didn't mean…

09:28.609 --> 09:30.278
Hey, I told you I was sorry.

09:31.904 --> 09:33.573
Good for you, but I'm not.

09:35.616 --> 09:38.995
Well, what can I do?
We're just so different.

09:40.663 --> 09:41.747
No! Not here!

09:48.170 --> 09:49.297
Go, go, go, go!

09:49.380 --> 09:50.506
- Hey, hey!
- Over there.

09:54.468 --> 09:55.344
Get up.

09:59.640 --> 10:01.892
Stop it. Hey!

10:07.940 --> 10:10.401
Oh, no, is she okay?

10:10.484 --> 10:11.944
Are you okay?

10:18.868 --> 10:20.828
He acts like a child.

10:21.662 --> 10:22.663
Teacher.

10:23.456 --> 10:24.373
I have a question.

10:24.457 --> 10:27.126
Would it be possible to solve that
if we apply L'Hôpital's rule?

10:28.753 --> 10:30.171
Teacher.

10:30.254 --> 10:31.589
Can I solve this problem

10:31.672 --> 10:34.133
using y as a derivative of the root x?

10:34.216 --> 10:35.259
- Teacher.
- Yes?

10:35.343 --> 10:36.719
- Teacher.
- All right, kids.

10:36.802 --> 10:39.055
- You can have your lunch break.
- Wait, teacher.

10:40.765 --> 10:43.809
- She can be super selfish.
- Teacher.

10:44.310 --> 10:45.811
THE UNBEARABLE LIGHTNESS OF BEING

10:47.438 --> 10:49.982
There's nothing I love more
than lying in the shade.

10:50.941 --> 10:52.485
I love the gentle breeze,

10:53.944 --> 10:55.780
the sunlight shining through the trees…

10:59.325 --> 11:00.785
You're so ridiculous.

11:03.329 --> 11:04.246
Leave me alone.

11:04.830 --> 11:07.458
Hurry. Finish that already,
so you can return it.

11:14.674 --> 11:16.842
This is great.

11:18.135 --> 11:20.721
To top it off, he's so lazy.

11:40.282 --> 11:41.158
Who was that?

11:42.952 --> 11:44.745
Choi Ung! You again?

11:45.621 --> 11:46.789
I thought I told you to be quiet!

11:48.499 --> 11:50.126
Things are already exhausting,

11:50.209 --> 11:52.586
but she has a talent for making it worse.

11:52.670 --> 11:56.382
The bottom line is,
he's a very pathetic guy.

11:59.844 --> 12:01.512
Sorry. What was the question?

12:01.595 --> 12:03.556
Why can't you focus?

12:05.391 --> 12:07.184
Oh, the things I hate?

12:07.768 --> 12:09.019
Kook Yeon-su.

12:11.689 --> 12:13.399
Kook Yeon-su.

12:13.482 --> 12:14.734
She's some silly girl I know.

12:14.817 --> 12:16.152
I hate pathetic beings.

12:16.235 --> 12:19.363
What I despise the most
are people who are hopelessly pathetic.

12:19.447 --> 12:21.407
Being selfish.
I hate selfish people who only--

12:21.490 --> 12:23.117
People who cause trouble for others.

12:23.200 --> 12:25.202
If you wanna fail,
then go fail on your own.

12:25.286 --> 12:26.954
Why do you have to
drag others down with you?

12:27.037 --> 12:29.790
Those who are harsh.
Or some people who talk without thinking.

12:29.874 --> 12:31.542
To me, they're super rude.

12:31.625 --> 12:33.335
Seriously, look who's talking.

12:33.419 --> 12:36.714
He should look in the mirror first,
because he just doesn't think at all.

12:36.797 --> 12:39.467
He? Are, are you talking about me?

12:39.550 --> 12:41.719
You started it.
You were bitching about me too.

12:41.802 --> 12:42.928
Wait, who? Me?

12:43.012 --> 12:44.054
Are you done talking?

12:44.138 --> 12:45.473
Not yet. Obviously still talking.

12:46.682 --> 12:49.143
Why did you want to film
this documentary again?

12:49.226 --> 12:52.271
It's a program that features
the top student helping the worst student.

12:52.354 --> 12:54.148
- Correct?
- Ah, I get it.

12:54.231 --> 12:56.358
I think you're trying to find out
how long regular people

12:56.442 --> 12:57.568
can endure anti-social ones.

12:57.651 --> 12:59.278
Putting the best
and worst student together,

12:59.361 --> 13:00.988
experiments like that are unethical.

13:01.071 --> 13:03.032
Speaking of the best student
and the worst student,

13:03.115 --> 13:05.242
from their titles,
who do you think is more anti-social?

13:05.326 --> 13:08.704
When people like her enter society,
they will exhaust everyone around them.

13:08.788 --> 13:11.165
- Trust me, I know this.
- Is that so?

13:11.248 --> 13:13.667
Well, someone like you wouldn't even
be able to participate in society.

13:13.751 --> 13:15.127
So how could you know that?

13:17.630 --> 13:19.173
Here's another question.

13:19.256 --> 13:21.801
What do you think
you'll be doing after ten years?

13:25.679 --> 13:28.098
In ten years, I'll be 29.

13:29.475 --> 13:33.604
I'm pretty sure I'd still be good
at whatever it is that I'm doing.

13:33.687 --> 13:37.233
I guess I want to live a peaceful life
without doing anything.

13:37.316 --> 13:38.901
I'll be leading
groups of people in my company,

13:38.984 --> 13:40.778
plus, I'll be living an active life.

13:40.861 --> 13:41.821
A successful one.

13:42.404 --> 13:44.782
I hope I'll be able to live a quiet life.

13:44.865 --> 13:47.076
- One thing's for sure…
- One thing I know for sure is--

13:47.159 --> 13:49.620
…I'd have nothing to do
with this pathetic person beside me.

13:50.204 --> 13:52.331
That's exactly how I feel.

13:55.626 --> 13:57.753
THE BEST AND WORST STUDENTS
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

13:57.837 --> 13:59.296
VIEWS

13:59.380 --> 14:00.381
DOCUMENTARIES

14:04.343 --> 14:05.302
LEAVING A REPLY BECAUSE NO ONE WOULD

14:06.554 --> 14:07.638
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

14:12.935 --> 14:14.687
TRENDING VIDEO
SO FUNNY

14:22.528 --> 14:23.988
AMAZING CHEMISTRY
HILARIOUS

14:25.489 --> 14:28.033
THIS IS A MUST WATCH
PLEASE LET THERE BE A SECOND SEASON

14:36.166 --> 14:38.335
EPISODE 1
I KNOW WHAT YOU DID LAST SUMMER

14:41.130 --> 14:42.214
This isn't it.

14:42.298 --> 14:43.132
THE PRESENT

14:43.215 --> 14:44.550
Ms. Kook Yeon-su?

14:45.718 --> 14:46.927
Yes?

14:47.011 --> 14:50.639
So far, I'm not seeing or hearing anything
that's worth listening to. Is that it?

14:50.723 --> 14:54.393
I definitely didn't think
that this is the life I'd lead.

14:55.603 --> 14:57.855
I hope you'll listen
until the end of my presentation

14:57.938 --> 14:59.940
before you make that conclusion.

15:00.024 --> 15:01.859
Fine, go on. Continue.

15:01.942 --> 15:04.862
First, allow me to explain
the online promotion methods.

15:04.945 --> 15:08.157
We believed one of the methods of gaining
people's interest before the opening

15:08.657 --> 15:12.369
is through online campaigns and
organizing various participation events.

15:12.453 --> 15:13.996
After we use hashtag events, the brand--

15:14.079 --> 15:15.122
Stop, Ms. Kook.

15:15.706 --> 15:17.207
This is quite disappointing.

15:17.291 --> 15:19.251
This isn't what we asked
your group to work on.

15:19.335 --> 15:21.128
You should have checked
with me before you did this.

15:21.211 --> 15:24.131
We have no interest
in launching this brand with clichés.

15:24.214 --> 15:25.841
Our main goal is to capture

15:25.925 --> 15:27.593
our target market's attention
for the store opening.

15:27.676 --> 15:28.928
We found that generating--

15:29.011 --> 15:30.638
Do you honestly think
I'm not aware of that?

15:31.221 --> 15:33.265
- But sir, this time we--
- Your company's called "Run".

15:33.349 --> 15:34.475
You may be a small company,

15:34.558 --> 15:36.936
but recently you've been raking
in quite a lot of awards,

15:37.019 --> 15:39.355
and I heard your team
is the most skilled in the industry.

15:40.189 --> 15:42.107
But I think that your work is lame.

15:42.191 --> 15:45.069
If anything, I do respect
how you've built such a decent image.

15:46.070 --> 15:48.822
Ji-hyeon. The presentation this afternoon…

15:48.906 --> 15:50.950
- Can you move it earlier to 10 a.m.?
- Yes, sir.

15:51.533 --> 15:53.369
- Excuse me, Mr. Jang?
- Yes? That's it, right?

15:53.452 --> 15:54.703
Is there anything else?

15:54.787 --> 15:59.416
Getting looked down on like this
was unfortunately never part of my plan.

15:59.500 --> 16:03.212
- Yes. I'm not done yet.
- All right. Hurry up, then.

16:11.345 --> 16:13.973
To open Soen Shop,
we are planning to make it unique,

16:14.056 --> 16:15.933
by collaborating with artists.

16:16.016 --> 16:18.519
Using merch to attract customers
is terribly cliché.

16:18.602 --> 16:21.772
Plus if we go for those marketing methods,
they can be expensive, yet ineffective.

16:21.855 --> 16:23.649
Consumers don't fall for--

16:24.316 --> 16:28.362
Didn't you tell us you'd listen
until the end? Or have you forgotten?

16:30.072 --> 16:31.073
Go ahead.

16:31.865 --> 16:35.035
Our strategy is not to sell merchandise
through our collaboration.

16:35.119 --> 16:37.705
We're planning on creating
the merch on Soen Shop,

16:37.788 --> 16:39.581
and this is what we'll be promoting.

16:41.792 --> 16:43.544
These are the works of Go-oh,

16:43.627 --> 16:45.587
who's the most
popular illustrator these days.

16:45.671 --> 16:46.797
Go-oh is known for drawing

16:46.880 --> 16:49.842
detailed and trendy pieces
based on building structures.

16:49.925 --> 16:52.511
And recently,
Go-oh received more attention

16:52.594 --> 16:54.972
as the idol singer NJ
bought one of his works.

16:55.055 --> 16:56.890
The collaboration we're proposing is,

16:56.974 --> 17:00.602
we tempt this artist to do a live drawing
for the opening ceremony.

17:01.645 --> 17:03.022
You may continue.

17:03.105 --> 17:05.315
Go-oh is a talented artist
who's into detail,

17:05.399 --> 17:06.984
he makes unique and innovative drawings.

17:07.067 --> 17:11.071
His vibe is a perfect match for Soen Shop,
since that's what the brand is all about.

17:11.155 --> 17:14.450
Go-oh already has a large and loyal
fanbase because of his unique drawings

17:14.533 --> 17:16.076
and sincere attitude towards the art.

17:16.160 --> 17:17.745
That's why, if we promote the shop

17:17.828 --> 17:19.496
featuring his drawings
on the exterior wall,

17:19.580 --> 17:21.832
it'll make Soen Shop a trendy
and popular place

17:21.915 --> 17:24.126
people will be lining up to visit.

17:31.175 --> 17:33.510
Can you really get the artist on board?

17:33.594 --> 17:35.179
Of course, sir. We'll close this deal.

17:35.262 --> 17:37.222
Yes, better make sure you do, then.

17:40.642 --> 17:42.102
Not bad at all.

17:42.186 --> 17:43.312
I have no idea why you waited

17:43.395 --> 17:45.397
until the very last minute
to show us that proposal.

17:45.481 --> 17:47.608
- The presentations was--
- That'll be all.

18:02.664 --> 18:06.210
Ms. Kook. You were so great.
You kept your cool the whole time.

18:06.293 --> 18:09.338
Gosh. I've heard horror stories
about Mr. Jang's aggressiveness,

18:09.421 --> 18:11.048
but I didn't imagine he'd be that scary.

18:11.131 --> 18:12.341
He was being mean on purpose.

18:12.424 --> 18:15.469
Making us come in early in the morning,
ordering us around all the time.

18:15.552 --> 18:17.262
He kept cutting her off
when she was talking.

18:17.346 --> 18:19.473
But still, this project
is a done deal, right?

18:19.556 --> 18:20.933
Yeah, tell us, Ms. Kook.

18:21.016 --> 18:23.435
Can we really
get the artist to work with us?

18:24.061 --> 18:27.314
I thought we haven't been able
to confirm anything from his side yet.

18:27.898 --> 18:29.650
That jerk's unbelievable.

18:36.156 --> 18:37.491
When we get back to the office,

18:37.574 --> 18:39.660
get me all the data
you can find on the artist.

18:39.743 --> 18:42.121
Everything from his posts on social media
to his interviews.

18:42.204 --> 18:45.374
No matter what happens,
we have to close this deal.

18:45.457 --> 18:49.169
That might be hard, since the artist
has never revealed himself to the public.

18:49.253 --> 18:52.005
Nobody's seen his face,
not even at exhibitions.

18:52.089 --> 18:55.134
I'm going to find him,
I'll do whatever it takes.

18:58.554 --> 19:01.014
Cutting people off
while they're explaining something?

19:01.098 --> 19:03.183
Did that jerk grow up
without learning any manners?

19:03.892 --> 19:05.519
Jeez, where is my car?

19:24.329 --> 19:25.998
Oh, it's you, Mr. Jang.

19:26.582 --> 19:29.001
Was there something
you wanted to talk to me about?

19:30.919 --> 19:33.046
What are you doing
opening my car door for me?

19:33.672 --> 19:34.673
What?

19:41.722 --> 19:42.973
So sorry about that.

19:43.056 --> 19:45.184
I haven't gotten used
to my company car yet.

19:45.267 --> 19:46.560
I was mistaken.

19:48.729 --> 19:50.606
- By the way, Ms. Kook.
- Yes?

19:50.689 --> 19:52.858
I hate people who are all bark.

19:52.941 --> 19:55.777
In fact, I think irresponsible people
are the most pathetic.

19:56.695 --> 19:59.072
- Right.
- I seriously hope you weren't bluffing

19:59.156 --> 20:01.408
about getting the artist
to work on this project.

20:01.491 --> 20:04.036
You can't possibly
be that pathetic, can you?

20:19.593 --> 20:21.094
Although it's been ten years…

20:21.178 --> 20:22.262
What an asshole.

20:22.346 --> 20:25.057
…I never imagined
I'd hear those familiar words again.

20:25.807 --> 20:27.893
but from another person at this age.

20:36.235 --> 20:38.987
I have always known this.

20:39.738 --> 20:41.782
I knew that I would live a peaceful life.

20:45.702 --> 20:48.497
See, I've always dreamed of this.

20:48.580 --> 20:49.873
Going back to the beginning.

20:49.957 --> 20:52.918
We started this restaurant
for drivers passing by.

20:53.001 --> 20:53.919
- Cut.
- Huh?

20:54.002 --> 20:56.046
Sorry about that, but it's Ung.
What's he doing back there?

20:56.129 --> 20:58.590
You need to stop
making those weird movements.

20:58.674 --> 21:00.968
I have to film Dad, but since you're
moving around a lot, you're distracting.

21:01.051 --> 21:03.762
Come on! I was on a roll,
and you ruined a perfectly good shot.

21:03.845 --> 21:06.348
It's your fault we need to start again.
Go inside and stop bothering us.

21:06.431 --> 21:08.642
- No way, I was sitting in this spot first.
- Go on!

21:08.725 --> 21:11.019
I thought I'd be fine talking
in front of the camera,

21:11.103 --> 21:12.604
but this is making me real nervous.

21:12.688 --> 21:15.691
To be honest, I wouldn't mind
having some more peace in my life.

21:15.774 --> 21:18.068
…started with Ung about 25 years ago.

21:18.151 --> 21:20.946
We started as a diner
for drivers back then.

21:21.029 --> 21:25.534
Uh, our specialties are steamed fish,
also, there's chicken feet.

21:25.617 --> 21:27.703
You know we even went viral for our--

21:27.786 --> 21:29.621
- Hey, aren't you done yet?
- You ruined my shot!

21:29.705 --> 21:31.456
How could you bother him?
You know he's so busy.

21:31.540 --> 21:33.458
Ji-ung, shouldn't you
be at work or something?

21:33.542 --> 21:36.962
- It's all right. I'm not too busy.
- Eat before you go. Come inside.

21:37.045 --> 21:39.089
- I'm sorry about that.
- No! You can't.

21:39.172 --> 21:42.175
- Ung, stop loafing around, you're so lazy.
- Finish this, all of it.

21:42.259 --> 21:44.136
Hold on, why are you always
ordering me around?

21:44.219 --> 21:45.137
What if I'm busy too?

21:45.220 --> 21:46.888
- You? Busy?
- Stop talking nonsense.

21:46.972 --> 21:49.224
When were you ever busy?
You're not even working.

21:49.308 --> 21:50.851
- Hey, put that away.
- Don't say that.

21:50.934 --> 21:52.853
He's spending
his precious time helping us.

21:52.936 --> 21:54.771
You should be thanking him
for doing your job.

21:54.855 --> 21:56.398
- Jerk.
- You little brat.

21:56.481 --> 21:59.776
As soon as you're done here,
man the counter. And don't just disappear.

21:59.860 --> 22:01.778
- Honey, please help me with something.
- All right, then.

22:01.862 --> 22:04.239
- I can't do it by myself.
- Oh, I'd better go.

22:04.323 --> 22:05.490
- Sure.
- Be right back, okay?

22:06.992 --> 22:08.952
I told you to stop filming, you ass.

22:09.036 --> 22:12.289
You'd better stop if you don't wanna
lose your fingers or the camera.

22:12.831 --> 22:14.750
Hey, what the heck
happened to your face?

22:15.667 --> 22:18.295
Even pork needs to be marinated
for eight hours.

22:18.378 --> 22:19.755
What are you talking about?

22:19.838 --> 22:21.465
I only slept
two and a half hours last night.

22:21.548 --> 22:23.133
Didn't even rest as much as pork.

22:23.216 --> 22:24.051
That sucks.

22:24.134 --> 22:27.095
You sleep and poop as much as pigs do,
so it's kind of balanced.

22:27.179 --> 22:29.431
Oh, shut up. Quit recording me!

22:30.057 --> 22:32.559
But I was told to film you
for the promotional video.

22:32.642 --> 22:33.727
Don't even think about it.

22:33.810 --> 22:35.645
- Not on your life.
- Hey, Ung!

22:35.729 --> 22:36.646
Yeah?

22:37.230 --> 22:38.190
Ung.

22:38.815 --> 22:41.151
Over here, sweetie. Look at the camera.

22:42.027 --> 22:43.278
That's right.

22:44.363 --> 22:45.906
Oh, how cute.

22:51.078 --> 22:52.496
Ung! Look at Mommy.

22:52.579 --> 22:53.413
Ung! Over here.

22:53.497 --> 22:55.415
- Look at your teacher.
- Look at the camera.

22:56.333 --> 22:58.210
Look at your teacher. Yes, good.

22:58.293 --> 23:00.045
Look over there. Don't look at me.

23:05.509 --> 23:07.302
"Choi Ung"?

23:07.386 --> 23:08.637
Yes. My name is Choi Ung.

23:08.720 --> 23:09.763
And you? What's your name?

23:10.347 --> 23:11.890
I'm not gonna tell you.

23:15.227 --> 23:16.269
KIM JI-UNG

23:16.353 --> 23:17.562
Not you. I meant Ji-ung.

23:17.646 --> 23:19.689
- Would you like some stew?
- Yes, I'd love that.

23:19.773 --> 23:20.982
Did you forget your son, Mom?

23:21.066 --> 23:22.484
Fine, you can have some too.

23:23.318 --> 23:26.446
Hey, I have an idea
how we can improve the shoot.

23:26.530 --> 23:29.116
I'll practice the lines I'll say,
so we can go faster.

23:29.199 --> 23:30.033
If it's okay.

23:30.117 --> 23:32.411
Would it be okay with you
to do this again when you're free?

23:32.494 --> 23:34.079
- I'm never too busy for you guys.
- Really?

23:34.162 --> 23:35.789
So call me anytime you wanna do it.

23:35.872 --> 23:37.541
Thank you so much.

23:37.624 --> 23:40.919
Wow. It feels really good
to have a producer who helps out.

23:41.002 --> 23:42.838
When else would I be able to do this?

23:44.840 --> 23:47.050
What now? Stop looking at me like that.

23:47.134 --> 23:49.177
The cabbages are arriving later.

23:49.261 --> 23:52.055
Bring them inside.
Don't even think of disappearing on us.

23:52.848 --> 23:55.809
I hope you're not forgetting
that I'm your flesh and blood, old man.

23:56.893 --> 23:59.146
- I'll prepare two bowls.
- All right, thanks.

24:00.147 --> 24:03.859
Dude, it seems like you'll be the one
inheriting the restaurant later.

24:03.942 --> 24:06.445
My parents are acting
like you're their son these days.

24:06.528 --> 24:09.281
Right, it's quite obvious…

24:09.364 --> 24:11.575
that if it were a choice,
I would be the better son.

24:11.658 --> 24:12.659
Dream on.

24:12.742 --> 24:13.910
How come you're not at work?

24:13.994 --> 24:16.121
Why do you keep coming back here
and threatening my status

24:16.204 --> 24:17.122
as the only heir, huh?

24:17.205 --> 24:19.958
Hey, I just finished a program,
and I barely got a break.

24:20.041 --> 24:23.044
I'm gonna be super busy again
when I start my next project.

24:23.128 --> 24:24.171
So that's why…

24:24.796 --> 24:26.256
I should have fun here before that.

24:26.339 --> 24:29.217
Hey! Stop! Why'd you do that?

24:29.301 --> 24:31.094
- Nothing, I'm having fun.
- Come here!

24:31.178 --> 24:34.014
Oh! Mom, Dad, look at him,
he's gonna ruin the bean sprouts that way!

24:34.097 --> 24:35.348
- Put that down!
- I wasn't--

24:35.432 --> 24:36.808
Put it down right now.

24:37.309 --> 24:38.727
- Hey! Stop that!
- Why the heck…

24:38.810 --> 24:40.645
Wait till I get my hands on you!

24:40.729 --> 24:42.147
- Put the bean sprouts down!
- It wasn't me!

24:42.230 --> 24:44.316
I can't believe
you're fooling around with food!

24:44.399 --> 24:46.193
Truth is, for some reason

24:46.276 --> 24:49.321
I thought my life would be
a bit more mature by this point.

24:49.863 --> 24:51.990
Ms. Kook and Mr. Jang are so alike,

24:52.073 --> 24:53.992
and that's why
they keep clashing with each other.

24:54.075 --> 24:56.536
I had so much fun
watching them argue from the front row.

24:56.620 --> 24:59.915
So true. You saw how Ms. Kook reacted
when Mr. Jang cut her off

24:59.998 --> 25:01.625
in the middle of her presentation, right?

25:02.417 --> 25:05.587
"Didn't you tell us you'd listen
until the end, or have you forgotten?"

25:05.670 --> 25:06.588
Unbelievable.

25:06.671 --> 25:09.090
I think Ms. Kook was so cool.
Don't you agree?

25:09.174 --> 25:10.008
Super cool.

25:10.091 --> 25:13.053
Besides, that project isn't something
a small company like ours can easily get.

25:13.136 --> 25:15.180
Yet she was able
to give us a fighting chance.

25:15.263 --> 25:17.724
She's almost like
the breadwinner of this family.

25:17.807 --> 25:19.100
Like our CEO's good luck charm.

25:19.684 --> 25:22.312
Imagine, how crazy would it be
to get on her bad side.

25:22.896 --> 25:25.690
She's so fearless when
she's facing our demanding clients,

25:25.774 --> 25:27.817
but then if she ever gets angry at us…

25:27.901 --> 25:30.487
Polar bears tear people apart
with their paws,

25:30.570 --> 25:32.322
but Ms. Kook tears people
apart with her words…

25:32.405 --> 25:33.532
How is it going, Ms. Kook?

25:33.615 --> 25:36.368
Everyone, about the information
on Go-oh that I asked for,

25:36.451 --> 25:38.036
can you please give me an update by three?

25:38.119 --> 25:39.329
- Yes, ma'am.
- Okay.

25:43.250 --> 25:45.293
What's going on, guys? What are you up to?

25:45.377 --> 25:46.336
What's going on here?

25:46.419 --> 25:48.338
Why are you guys
so good at everything you do?

25:48.421 --> 25:50.298
I heard your project
was given the green light.

25:50.382 --> 25:52.342
Oh, my jaw almost dropped to the floor.

25:52.425 --> 25:54.010
Good work, everyone.

25:54.094 --> 25:57.430
But most especially, Ms. Kook,
who succeeded once again.

25:57.514 --> 25:58.515
Wow.

25:58.598 --> 26:00.183
So, seems like
we should go out and celebrate--

26:00.267 --> 26:01.810
We can't have any gatherings.

26:01.893 --> 26:03.645
I'm not suggesting a gathering,
of course not.

26:03.728 --> 26:06.064
Why would we do that?
That suggestion is totally crazy.

26:06.147 --> 26:08.525
We shouldn't even be having
company gatherings, right?

26:08.608 --> 26:09.568
We all hate them.

26:10.694 --> 26:11.861
Anyway, what do you think of dinner--

26:11.945 --> 26:13.780
Sorry, but I'm already
going out with my mom.

26:13.863 --> 26:17.242
Oh, so sudden?
Or are you just making an excuse?

26:17.325 --> 26:18.368
No, that's not it.

26:18.451 --> 26:20.912
What I meant to say was,
it'll be hard if we leave at that time.

26:20.996 --> 26:22.789
You think, we should go have lunch now?

26:22.872 --> 26:25.917
But we've already eaten lunch, sir.

26:28.712 --> 26:30.714
- What do you mean?
- I just remembered

26:30.797 --> 26:33.883
that the three of us had our lunch
when we stepped out of the office earlier.

26:36.511 --> 26:37.596
You did?

26:37.679 --> 26:39.723
How, how come you didn't tell me?

26:39.806 --> 26:42.559
How could we? You weren't able
to go to the presentation with us

26:42.642 --> 26:44.102
because you had a stomachache.

26:44.185 --> 26:46.730
We jumped to the conclusion
that you wouldn't be able to join us.

26:46.813 --> 26:49.482
That's all right, smart thinking.

26:49.566 --> 26:50.734
Thanks, sir.

26:50.817 --> 26:53.778
Then if you can't go out for dinner,
and you've already had lunch,

26:53.862 --> 26:55.614
- how are we supposed to--
- Well, in that case,

26:55.697 --> 26:57.198
coffee! How about coffee?

26:57.282 --> 26:58.491
- Yeah.
- Coffee sounds great.

26:59.075 --> 27:00.660
- You all have coffee.
- Oh, yeah.

27:01.369 --> 27:02.829
You have a cup too.

27:02.912 --> 27:04.748
Looks like you all have, except for me.

27:04.831 --> 27:06.041
- Oh, yeah.
- Okay.

27:06.708 --> 27:09.085
- But, sir, why don't I get you porridge?
- No, no need.

27:10.128 --> 27:12.297
- Sit down.
- I hate porridge.

27:13.715 --> 27:15.091
He sounded upset.

27:27.479 --> 27:29.314
SOL-I

27:35.528 --> 27:42.535
SEOUL HARDWARE STORE

28:27.497 --> 28:29.040
OUR SUMMER CHRISTMAS TREE

30:11.434 --> 30:12.435
Hello?

30:12.519 --> 30:14.771
Finally!
Why weren't you picking up?

30:17.232 --> 30:20.235
Why were you ignoring my calls? Why?

30:20.318 --> 30:21.736
Come on!

30:21.820 --> 30:22.904
Can't you see I'm busy working?

30:22.987 --> 30:25.114
There's a reason
why people have cellphones.

30:25.824 --> 30:26.991
Fine, whatever…

30:27.075 --> 30:28.159
What?

30:29.160 --> 30:30.119
- What are you…
- Get up.

30:30.203 --> 30:31.538
Wait, what do you think you're doing?

30:31.621 --> 30:32.831
Get up. Time to exercise.

30:32.914 --> 30:34.332
Stop! Why are you being so annoying?

30:34.415 --> 30:36.835
Just get up. You told me
you haven't been sleeping well.

30:36.918 --> 30:40.046
Ow, ow, ow. Jerk! Let go of my arm!

30:40.129 --> 30:42.131
You know what my job is as your manager?

30:42.215 --> 30:43.967
I need to take care
of my artist's health too.

30:46.427 --> 30:49.389
I'm already exhausted,
why do I have to do this?

30:49.472 --> 30:51.724
Aren't I a great manager?
I'm the kindest ever.

30:51.808 --> 30:52.934
You're fired.

30:53.017 --> 30:54.519
That would count as wrongful dismissal.

30:54.602 --> 30:57.272
Hurry, you only need to
make it over there. You can do it.

30:57.355 --> 30:58.356
I'm so tired.

30:58.439 --> 31:00.275
Don't stop, keep going. Come on.

31:00.358 --> 31:02.443
One, two, three, four.

31:02.527 --> 31:03.903
Two, two, three, four.

31:05.071 --> 31:06.531
Get over here, hurry up.

31:06.614 --> 31:08.032
Hurry! You can do it.

31:08.116 --> 31:09.909
It's the flag. Make the goal.

31:10.743 --> 31:13.246
- All right, we're here!
- Yeah, goal!

31:15.999 --> 31:18.209
You guys think of the stupidest things.

31:18.293 --> 31:20.628
It's cause I heard
you only slept two hours.

31:20.712 --> 31:22.672
Did you really
have to tell him about that?

31:22.755 --> 31:24.507
- Who? Me? Here, catch.
- Oh.

31:25.049 --> 31:27.844
Why are you always hanging around?
Did you get fired or something?

31:27.927 --> 31:30.388
Hey, if you're talented
you're allowed to slack off, hm?

31:31.389 --> 31:32.599
By the way,

31:32.682 --> 31:35.518
isn't it time you tell your parents
who you are in the art world?

31:35.602 --> 31:37.478
What for? They already know I draw a lot.

31:37.562 --> 31:39.772
They called me a while ago,
and they sounded worried about you.

31:39.856 --> 31:41.482
They asked if you could earn a living.

31:41.566 --> 31:43.484
They searched your name online
and couldn't find any hit.

31:43.568 --> 31:44.986
You didn't give them any kind of details?

31:45.069 --> 31:47.780
How much do you earn anyway?
Tell me, I'm not gonna judge you.

31:47.864 --> 31:49.782
Wow, I can't believe
you don't wanna tell your parents.

31:49.866 --> 31:51.868
You don't have to be super secretive.

31:51.951 --> 31:53.786
- Hey!
- Wow, hey!

31:53.870 --> 31:55.204
- Jeez, man.
- You shook it!

31:55.288 --> 31:57.498
Of course not. Just tell me,
how much does he earn?

31:58.166 --> 32:01.127
All right. Each drawing
is worth 50 million won.

32:01.210 --> 32:03.338
- That much? For real?
- Hmm.

32:03.421 --> 32:05.006
Wow. What an asshole.

32:05.632 --> 32:06.549
Hey.

32:06.633 --> 32:09.427
You're using that as an excuse
to cuss me out, aren't you?

32:09.510 --> 32:10.511
Of course not.

32:10.595 --> 32:11.721
- You asshole.
- What?

32:11.804 --> 32:13.139
What? Sorry.

32:13.222 --> 32:14.599
Yeah, before I forget.

32:14.682 --> 32:16.476
I told dad you disappeared
before bothering to move the cabbages.

32:16.559 --> 32:18.102
He said he'll kill you tomorrow.

32:27.153 --> 32:29.739
Don't you think
the weather is so nice tonight?

32:38.831 --> 32:39.874
- Oh, shit!
- Jeez!

32:39.958 --> 32:42.418
Seriously, you're a bunch of idiots.

32:42.502 --> 32:43.711
- You shook these, didn't you?
- No.

32:43.795 --> 32:45.838
Didn't you see?
Same thing happened to my drink.

32:45.922 --> 32:47.048
I didn't shake them.

32:47.131 --> 32:48.925
- Admit it, did you?
- No way.

32:50.927 --> 32:52.971
I know you.
You're ignoring me again, aren't you?

32:56.307 --> 32:57.350
You're such a jerk.

32:59.435 --> 33:00.311
Looks like…

33:00.395 --> 33:01.354
…I'm your only customer.

33:01.437 --> 33:03.147
- You'll go under soon.
- Hey!

33:03.231 --> 33:04.607
You startled me.

33:04.691 --> 33:06.859
I can hear you fine
even if you whisper, you know.

33:06.943 --> 33:10.530
Hey. Do you know how many times
you've bailed on this poor guy?

33:11.990 --> 33:13.157
- Three?
- Four times.

33:13.741 --> 33:16.244
Do you have some kind of grudge
against him and haven't told me?

33:16.327 --> 33:18.746
How could I when I've never
even seen him before.

33:18.830 --> 33:22.208
And yet, you stood him up
when he went to your office building.

33:22.291 --> 33:24.502
He even took the time
to go there during your lunch break

33:24.585 --> 33:26.587
because you said
you were so busy that time.

33:26.671 --> 33:28.047
I totally forgot.

33:28.131 --> 33:30.883
You really are a scumbag.

33:30.967 --> 33:32.927
How can you be so mean to other people?

33:33.011 --> 33:35.722
How can you function as a member
of society like that?

33:36.764 --> 33:39.559
People worse than me
are living normal lives in society.

33:39.642 --> 33:42.395
Just shut up.
That guy you ghosted for four times,

33:42.478 --> 33:44.105
he must be totally smitten with you.

33:44.188 --> 33:46.566
He keeps saying
he really wants to meet you.

33:46.649 --> 33:48.526
Oh, I feel so sorry for him.

33:48.609 --> 33:50.319
- Really?
- For real.

33:50.403 --> 33:53.114
Will you cut it out?
You're going to meet with him this time.

33:53.197 --> 33:54.073
You can't vanish like before.

33:54.157 --> 33:56.034
If you bail on him again,
our friendship's over.

33:56.117 --> 33:57.827
Okay, fine. I'll meet him.

33:59.120 --> 34:00.538
I'm so sick of this.

34:00.621 --> 34:02.206
It's not that I'm forcing you to date.

34:02.290 --> 34:03.958
But you should meet other guys.

34:04.042 --> 34:05.418
That's all I'm asking you to do.

34:05.501 --> 34:07.795
Office, home, and here.
Office, home, and here.

34:07.879 --> 34:10.506
When I look into your eyes,
it's like I'm looking at a machine.

34:10.590 --> 34:12.300
There's no soul under your skin.

34:13.384 --> 34:14.469
Pork skin!

34:15.136 --> 34:16.554
I want pork skin. I'm suddenly craving it.

34:16.637 --> 34:18.765
It's like talking to a wall.

34:19.432 --> 34:21.726
We need to replenish our souls.

34:21.809 --> 34:24.145
How am I meeting guys replenish my soul?

34:24.228 --> 34:25.938
Forget it. I'm just going to work.

34:26.022 --> 34:28.649
- Then go out with someone at work.
- Ew. That's a terrible thing to say.

34:28.733 --> 34:30.693
You're making me lose my appetite.

34:30.777 --> 34:31.903
Could it be…

34:32.987 --> 34:34.906
You still haven't got over
that ex of yours.

34:34.989 --> 34:36.449
I'm just going to leave

34:36.532 --> 34:37.533
if you keep bringing him up.

34:37.617 --> 34:39.702
- Okay, see you.
- All right, I'll shut up. Okay, I'm sorry.

34:39.786 --> 34:42.163
Please sit down. Sit. I'm really sorry.

34:43.372 --> 34:45.583
You're making such a big deal out of it.

34:53.257 --> 34:56.344
I'm gonna take a break. Jeez, man.

34:56.928 --> 34:58.012
Why are you so lame?

34:58.096 --> 34:59.263
Let's see you do better then.

35:03.601 --> 35:05.520
Hey, Ung, about that live drawing show--

35:05.603 --> 35:06.729
Nope, no way.

35:06.813 --> 35:08.481
So stubborn.

35:08.564 --> 35:10.858
Why are you so obsessed
with keeping your identity a secret?

35:10.942 --> 35:12.276
You're living in the 20th century.

35:12.360 --> 35:14.529
Everything is about
communicating with others these days.

35:14.612 --> 35:16.447
You know he's not suited
for that kind of stuff.

35:16.531 --> 35:17.615
He can't even talk properly.

35:17.698 --> 35:19.200
Come on, I really don't get it.

35:19.283 --> 35:20.785
Five years ago, all you did was draw,

35:20.868 --> 35:23.246
saying that you were going to succeed
no matter what it takes.

35:23.329 --> 35:26.165
But now you're rejecting opportunities.
Where's the logic in that?

35:26.249 --> 35:29.418
He's successful, so he's changed.
Now he's so full of himself.

35:29.502 --> 35:31.587
- Hey.
- Dude, you shouldn't be so arrogant.

35:31.671 --> 35:33.881
You know what?
I heard Nu-a is collaborating with SJ.

35:33.965 --> 35:35.091
So who's Nu-a?

35:35.174 --> 35:37.927
An artist who has
almost the same style as him.

35:38.010 --> 35:39.846
Nu-a's like his… rival.

35:41.264 --> 35:43.141
"Rival"? What?

35:43.224 --> 35:46.269
Hey, that Nu-a's been copying me.

35:46.352 --> 35:49.272
At this rate, people will think that Nu-a
was first and that you're the copycat.

35:49.355 --> 35:51.190
Like no matter what I do,
you keep going back to the old days.

35:51.274 --> 35:53.109
You're the one
who keeps bringing up the past.

35:53.192 --> 35:55.444
It's motivation.
I want you to get motivated.

35:55.528 --> 35:57.321
Do you seriously wanna live like before?

35:57.989 --> 35:58.948
Jeez.

36:03.452 --> 36:05.329
Living in the past isn't that bad.

36:09.041 --> 36:10.251
What are you talking about?

36:15.298 --> 36:17.049
Hey.

36:18.217 --> 36:19.510
I'll make you a bet.

36:19.594 --> 36:20.887
If you get 15 points,

36:21.387 --> 36:23.556
tomorrow I'll move the cabbages for you.

36:24.682 --> 36:25.683
You sure?

36:27.393 --> 36:28.436
- Let's go.
- Come on.

36:28.519 --> 36:30.605
You won't score a single point.

36:51.584 --> 36:53.461
Hello there, Ja-gyeong.

36:56.130 --> 36:59.175
Oh, no. You reek of alcohol.

36:59.258 --> 37:02.637
My goodness, don't tell me
you spent the whole night drinking alone.

37:02.720 --> 37:05.806
What I want is to make a doll
with your stomach.

37:05.890 --> 37:07.975
Then I can squeeze it every day.

37:08.059 --> 37:10.811
Oh, better get washed up
before you go to bed.

37:10.895 --> 37:12.480
You have to go to work tomorrow.

37:12.563 --> 37:15.233
I might be home late,
so you should sleep inside.

37:15.316 --> 37:17.526
You don't need to stay up
just to wait for me.

37:17.610 --> 37:19.987
I was out here because it was too hot.

37:20.071 --> 37:21.572
Now you go clean yourself up.

37:22.406 --> 37:24.075
Can you wash me, please?

37:24.742 --> 37:27.954
- Please wash me, Grandma.
- My goodness, you're such a silly child.

37:28.037 --> 37:31.082
- Give me a kiss.
- Wait a minute. What's with you?

37:31.165 --> 37:33.042
- Have you lost your mind?
- Only a quick peck!

37:33.125 --> 37:34.961
What has gotten into you?

37:35.044 --> 37:37.129
Oh, you stink, dear. Hurry, get up.

37:37.213 --> 37:41.092
My goodness.
You are unbelievable.

37:41.175 --> 37:43.177
How much have you had to drink anyway?

37:43.261 --> 37:44.679
Oh, my goodness.

38:01.279 --> 38:02.738
ARTIST GO-OH

38:05.491 --> 38:06.867
GO-OH'S SOLO EXHIBITION

38:08.452 --> 38:10.788
GO-OH, THE ILLUSTRATOR
WHO PAINTS BUILDINGS WITH SOUL

38:20.423 --> 38:22.341
WHAT EXCITES YOU THE MOST
ABOUT BUILDINGS?

38:25.261 --> 38:27.596
YOU DRAW NATURE AS WELL AS BUILDINGS
WHAT ARE YOUR INTERESTS?

38:27.680 --> 38:29.640
CAN YOU TELL US
ABOUT YOUR DRAWING PROCESS?

38:29.724 --> 38:33.269
WHY AREN'T THERE PEOPLE
IN YOUR DRAWINGS?

38:33.352 --> 38:36.897
I LOVE THINGS THAT DON'T CHANGE BUT
PEOPLE CHANGE OR DISAPPEAR OVER TIME

38:36.981 --> 38:40.943
THAT'S WHY THERE ARE NO PEOPLE
OR TIME IN MY WORKS

39:00.004 --> 39:02.006
Ji-ung, the boss has been looking for you.

39:02.089 --> 39:04.383
I know. He's been calling me
every ten minutes.

39:04.467 --> 39:05.801
You haven't gone home yet?

39:05.885 --> 39:06.886
Do I smell?

39:06.969 --> 39:08.262
How many days now?

39:08.346 --> 39:09.680
Four days straight.

39:09.764 --> 39:11.223
I thought I told you to go home.

39:11.307 --> 39:13.476
Don't make it a habit
to slava away in the editing room.

39:14.018 --> 39:16.729
Mr. Park said he couldn't
go home at all when he was an assistant.

39:16.812 --> 39:19.982
Stop. I'll repeat.
Don't listen to anything that guy says.

39:20.066 --> 39:21.776
He doesn't say anything
worth listening to.

39:23.819 --> 39:25.654
- Oh, and Chae-ran.
- Yeah.

39:25.738 --> 39:26.906
Work with me on my next project.

39:26.989 --> 39:28.949
Sure, but I'm not done
working with Mr. Park.

39:29.033 --> 39:30.534
It's fine. I'll steal you away.

39:36.540 --> 39:37.958
You were looking for me?

39:39.543 --> 39:41.420
It's about time.
What took you so long?

39:41.504 --> 39:43.214
Why aren't you reporting to work?

39:43.964 --> 39:45.674
I needed to take a proper break.

39:47.885 --> 39:49.553
Can I guess why you called me?

39:49.637 --> 39:51.722
You need me
to work my ass off for something.

39:52.306 --> 39:53.641
Don't be such a wiseass.

39:55.351 --> 39:56.852
I'm telling you in advance.

39:56.936 --> 39:59.105
I'm not doing documentaries
on people anymore.

39:59.897 --> 40:01.107
But why the hell not?

40:01.190 --> 40:02.358
They're all so boring.

40:02.441 --> 40:05.403
And I wanna do something
related to the environment.

40:05.486 --> 40:08.280
Environment my foot. Do you
have any idea how tough those are?

40:08.364 --> 40:09.865
Well, I think it'll be fun.

40:09.949 --> 40:12.701
I heard Yun-jin doesn't wanna do it.
Just give those assignments to me.

40:15.996 --> 40:18.499
Fine. You can have it.

40:20.000 --> 40:21.043
Hang on.

40:22.294 --> 40:23.671
What's going on?

40:23.754 --> 40:26.215
For real? Are you being serious?

40:26.298 --> 40:28.092
But do one on people first.

40:28.175 --> 40:30.386
Then I'll let you do it.
I swear it'll be the last time!

40:30.469 --> 40:32.054
I knew there was a catch.

40:32.138 --> 40:34.515
You've never given me
the assignments I wanted in the past.

40:34.598 --> 40:37.226
It's a really simple one.
Plus, it's not even a series.

40:37.309 --> 40:39.437
Well, in that case,
you can get someone else to do it.

40:39.520 --> 40:40.896
Producer Han would go for that.

40:42.231 --> 40:44.483
Hey. Watch this.

40:56.912 --> 41:00.416
Someone who loves me deeply,
you know, someone I can always be with--

41:00.499 --> 41:02.710
- Sounds like you need a dog.
- Oh, look at this!

41:02.793 --> 41:04.545
What? What are you freaking out about?

41:04.628 --> 41:06.297
What is it? What'd you find?

41:06.380 --> 41:07.673
I should have realized.

41:07.756 --> 41:09.091
So? You found Go-oh yet?

41:10.593 --> 41:12.970
- Don't mind her.
- Hey, isn't that Ms. Kook?

41:13.053 --> 41:14.430
Wow. I've seen these videos before.

41:14.513 --> 41:16.223
But I never
made the connection til right now.

41:16.307 --> 41:19.143
Is that really
the number of views?

41:19.226 --> 41:20.394
- That's incredible.
- Wow.

41:20.478 --> 41:22.563
Ms. Kook was pretty harsh back then too.

41:22.646 --> 41:24.982
Look at the way she talks,
it's exactly the same as Mr. Jang.

41:25.065 --> 41:27.651
Totally. But she seems
harsher in these videos.

41:27.735 --> 41:30.905
This kid's name is Ung. I remember
she was very mean to him.

41:31.489 --> 41:33.491
I think Ung is holding
his own against her.

41:33.574 --> 41:36.285
Those two would fight like crazy.
It's totally savage.

41:36.368 --> 41:37.953
But if my memory serves me right,

41:38.037 --> 41:40.372
it was Ms. Kook
who usually picked on Ung first.

41:40.456 --> 41:42.917
- Unbelievable.
- Is that so?

41:43.000 --> 41:43.834
- Totally.
- Right.

41:44.418 --> 41:48.380
I got the feeling that Ms. Kook
had a huge crush on Ung before.

41:52.218 --> 41:53.552
Ms. Kook.

41:54.220 --> 41:55.346
Hello, Ms. Kook.

41:55.429 --> 41:57.640
Ji-un, you know the thing I asked for…

41:57.723 --> 41:59.058
Ms. Kook, when did you…

41:59.141 --> 42:02.853
Do I really talk the same way as Mr. Jang?

42:03.437 --> 42:04.396
Who? You?

42:04.480 --> 42:08.025
As Mr. Jang? Of course not.
We think you talk much better than him.

42:08.108 --> 42:10.319
So you're saying
that I'm just as annoying as he is.

42:10.402 --> 42:13.155
No! Of course not!
The footage was misleading.

42:13.739 --> 42:14.865
I think the producers deliberately

42:14.949 --> 42:17.326
made you the "bitch" character
in these videos.

42:17.409 --> 42:19.787
That's right. Did you sue them
for what they did to your image?

42:19.870 --> 42:21.288
You should file a case against them.

42:21.372 --> 42:22.373
- She should.
- Yeah, am I right?

42:22.456 --> 42:24.583
What's going on here?
You checking something out?

42:24.667 --> 42:25.834
Is it something funny?

42:25.918 --> 42:28.087
Would any of you know
how to get stuff like that

42:28.170 --> 42:29.380
deleted permanently?

42:29.463 --> 42:31.006
Well, I think if it's
from a broadcast channel,

42:31.090 --> 42:33.008
- you should talk to them.
- Broadcast? What broadcast?

42:33.092 --> 42:34.885
Do you want me
to file a complaint against them?

42:34.969 --> 42:36.554
Are you guys gathering the data we need?

42:36.637 --> 42:39.515
Yes, of course, we're checking
everything there is out there on Go-oh.

42:39.598 --> 42:41.600
- What is it? Tell me, what's going on?
- It's nothing, sir.

42:41.684 --> 42:44.019
We have to present all we have
to the client next week.

42:44.103 --> 42:46.355
But it seems you have
lots of time on your hands.

42:48.566 --> 42:50.192
- Oh, and Ye-in.
- Yes?

42:50.276 --> 42:51.777
It was him. It wasn't me at all.

42:53.362 --> 42:55.781
- What do you mean?
- He picked the fights first.

42:56.365 --> 42:59.368
Just to be clear,
he was always the one who started it.

42:59.451 --> 43:02.371
Oh, I see.

43:02.454 --> 43:04.498
Well, I only meant that, I mean…

43:04.582 --> 43:06.166
What is it? Come on, just tell me.

43:06.250 --> 43:08.002
Go on, what's the story? Well?

43:08.085 --> 43:09.878
What is it? You know I won't tell.

43:09.962 --> 43:12.172
What's it about?
What happened, what? Just tell me.

43:15.342 --> 43:16.427
- I won't.
- You will.

43:16.510 --> 43:17.970
Why do you always say no right away?

43:18.554 --> 43:20.055
Why do I wanna be part of that again?

43:20.139 --> 43:21.307
Why not?

43:21.390 --> 43:23.350
See the number of views? And the comments?

43:23.434 --> 43:26.186
It's the most popular documentary
on our channel, you know that?

43:26.270 --> 43:28.063
That's nothing more
than a short-term trend, okay.

43:28.147 --> 43:30.524
And only kids would watch
that kind of content these days.

43:30.608 --> 43:32.735
You know what director's
keep saying these days?

43:32.818 --> 43:35.070
"We have to attract younger viewers."

43:35.154 --> 43:37.323
Can you come up with a better idea
to attract young viewers

43:37.406 --> 43:38.824
other than revisiting these people?

43:38.907 --> 43:41.076
Since when do we film something
for the sole purpose

43:41.160 --> 43:42.328
of attracting younger viewers?

43:42.411 --> 43:43.579
Why don't you just do it?

43:44.371 --> 43:48.667
Hey, do you know that those dating shows
of non-celebrities have become so popular?

43:49.793 --> 43:52.588
They're actually more interesting
that the drama's you'll find on TV.

43:53.213 --> 43:54.298
Look at this.

43:54.381 --> 43:57.009
There aren't any TV series
that are this good.

43:57.092 --> 44:00.679
If we show them how much
the personalities of these two kids

44:00.763 --> 44:02.181
have changed after ten years,

44:02.264 --> 44:04.433
it'll be epic. I guarantee you.

44:04.516 --> 44:07.311
And if we use this well,
we'll get a totally popular documentary.

44:07.394 --> 44:10.022
But why do I have to film it?
You're the one who made it before.

44:11.732 --> 44:13.275
I'm not as young as I once was.

44:13.859 --> 44:15.152
I'm old now.

44:15.235 --> 44:16.904
And besides…

44:20.866 --> 44:21.700
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

44:21.784 --> 44:23.035
Hey, Kim Ji-ung!

44:23.994 --> 44:26.330
You're perfect,
because you know them best.

44:26.413 --> 44:28.999
Do you still keep in touch with those two?

44:29.667 --> 44:32.044
How are they doing now?
Gosh, I really am so curious.

44:32.127 --> 44:33.879
After all, it's been ten years.

44:35.631 --> 44:36.882
I'm curious how they've changed.

44:49.144 --> 44:50.646
They're saying he's cute.

44:50.729 --> 44:51.730
That won't do.

44:52.314 --> 44:54.900
"I know that guy, Choi Ung."

44:55.567 --> 44:59.363
"I can attest to the fact
that he's still as weird

44:59.446 --> 45:02.616
as he was in the video."

45:02.700 --> 45:03.909
All right.

45:06.870 --> 45:08.789
Hey, Ung! Someone's calling you!

45:12.209 --> 45:13.252
Ung!

45:26.640 --> 45:27.766
Ung!

45:31.603 --> 45:34.022
Ung! Ung, Ung, Ung, Ung, Ung.

45:34.106 --> 45:35.816
Just tell him I'll move the cabbages soon.

45:35.899 --> 45:39.027
- Uh, no, that's, that's not why.
- Is it urgent?

45:39.528 --> 45:41.655
Take a look. Just look at it.

45:41.739 --> 45:43.365
Fine. What's gotten into you this time?

45:43.449 --> 45:44.450
Come on. Get it. Hurry!

45:44.533 --> 45:45.868
- Do something, man. Answer it!
- What?

45:46.660 --> 45:48.954
Come on, answer it already, you idiot.

45:49.580 --> 45:50.831
Yes, hello?

45:50.914 --> 45:52.958
It's so hard
to get in touch with you.

45:53.041 --> 45:55.711
I heard you work late at night,
but you still wouldn't pick up my calls.

45:55.794 --> 45:58.630
Then I was calling you this morning,
but you wouldn't pick up either.

45:58.714 --> 46:03.218
Oh, hey there, NJ. I wasn't expecting
you would call. How are you?

46:03.302 --> 46:05.637
Well, you're even busier
than most celebrities.

46:06.138 --> 46:08.390
But I guess things became more hectic,

46:08.474 --> 46:10.851
after articles about me
buying your piece got out.

46:10.934 --> 46:13.145
Oh, yeah. Actually, thank you.

46:13.228 --> 46:15.939
After your purchase, my work
has gotten a lot more interest.

46:16.023 --> 46:17.900
Is that all you're gonna say to me?

46:19.026 --> 46:21.653
I wanna see more
of the things you're working on right now.

46:22.404 --> 46:25.908
- What are you doing later?
- Oh, I'll be moving cabbages--

46:26.742 --> 46:27.785
What?

46:29.369 --> 46:31.455
You can't tell her that.

46:31.538 --> 46:34.374
Well, I'm actually moving cabbages--

46:34.458 --> 46:37.252
- Stop with the cabbages, idiot!
- Do you wanna meet up later today?

46:37.336 --> 46:39.213
I want to take a look around your studio.

46:39.296 --> 46:41.006
Oh, wait, today?

46:41.089 --> 46:44.802
That's right, today. I think
my shoot's going to end pretty early.

46:45.385 --> 46:46.345
Uh.

46:46.428 --> 46:47.471
Let her come.

46:47.554 --> 46:48.847
- Tell her to come over.
- All right.

46:48.931 --> 46:51.308
Just call me when you're done,
so I know when to expect you.

46:51.391 --> 46:53.811
- Okay. I'll call you later then.
- Bye.

46:58.315 --> 47:01.193
Oh, my God! This is crazy! Unbelievable!

47:03.779 --> 47:06.740
- You and NJ were keeping in touch?
- This is the first time.

47:06.824 --> 47:09.201
Tell me, Ung, when did you
exchange your numbers? When?

47:09.284 --> 47:11.537
Huh? She was the one
who asked for my number.

47:11.620 --> 47:14.081
Seriously, she asked for your number?
When was that?

47:14.164 --> 47:15.582
I don't remember. Calm down.
Get away from me.

47:15.666 --> 47:18.335
This is awesome!
I can't believe this is happening to us.

47:18.418 --> 47:20.504
Crazy. NJ calling Choi Ung?

47:20.587 --> 47:22.256
The world has really changed so much.

47:22.339 --> 47:23.924
Hold on…

47:24.758 --> 47:28.554
Do you think…
she was calling to get a free drawing?

47:29.096 --> 47:30.305
What?

47:30.389 --> 47:31.598
I mean…

47:32.432 --> 47:34.768
"Is that all you're gonna say to me?"
She asked…

47:34.852 --> 47:37.229
"I wanna see more of the things
you're working on right now."

47:37.312 --> 47:38.188
She said after.

47:38.730 --> 47:41.859
What if she's asking
for another piece for free?

47:42.693 --> 47:47.781
Ung. Did you know that NJ just bought
a building worth 15 billion won?

47:47.865 --> 47:50.200
Which is why, whatever she asks for,
just give it to her.

47:50.284 --> 47:52.911
Everything that catches her eye
in this studio, just give it to her.

47:52.995 --> 47:55.998
Just hand her your stuff.
Give her everything you've got.

47:56.081 --> 47:58.542
It's amazing.
NJ's really coming here?

47:59.084 --> 48:00.252
I can't believe it!

48:01.587 --> 48:04.214
- Hey, Ung, should I change?
- Wait, show me your hands.

48:05.340 --> 48:06.758
What for?

48:10.721 --> 48:11.555
Hey, listen to me.

48:11.638 --> 48:13.515
If you go through my stuff again,
I swear, I'll kill you.

48:13.599 --> 48:15.893
I might die before that.
My heart's about to burst.

48:15.976 --> 48:18.896
I've always been a huge fan since she was
a trainee. So give me a break.

48:18.979 --> 48:21.231
Don't you think it's going to look fake
when she comes here

48:21.315 --> 48:22.941
and sees you wearing a stupid suit?

48:23.567 --> 48:26.153
Oh, you're right.
Why didn't I think of that?

48:26.236 --> 48:27.821
- Darn it. What do I wear?
- Hey.

48:28.530 --> 48:29.823
I can't wear anything.

48:30.616 --> 48:31.617
What?

48:32.492 --> 48:33.619
Why are there two of these?

48:33.702 --> 48:35.412
- About that--
- It's too lame.

48:38.206 --> 48:39.625
No way.

48:39.708 --> 48:40.626
Are they couple shirts?

48:42.252 --> 48:44.087
Oh, man,
now you're looking so sad.

48:44.171 --> 48:45.213
Shut up.

48:45.297 --> 48:47.007
You really wore
matching t-shirts?

48:47.090 --> 48:48.592
That's kinda cute, Ung.

48:49.468 --> 48:51.219
Oh, a leather jacket.

48:52.512 --> 48:53.513
Would it be weird?

49:09.738 --> 49:11.657
Good evening.
Do you have a reservation?

49:11.740 --> 49:12.574
Yes.

49:26.838 --> 49:28.131
Is that you, Mr. Jang?

49:36.640 --> 49:39.142
So, this is pretty awkward.

49:39.226 --> 49:41.186
Why are you eating here all alone?

49:41.687 --> 49:43.605
Actually, I don't mind eating by myself.

49:43.689 --> 49:45.315
Excuse me,
the table you reserved is this way.

49:45.399 --> 49:46.858
Oh, right.

50:16.471 --> 50:19.099
Are you Kook Yeon-su?

50:19.182 --> 50:22.185
- Oh.
- I know, you're Choi Ung.

50:22.269 --> 50:25.564
Yeah, I saw you in that documentary.
You're the worst student.

50:26.606 --> 50:29.317
- That's not me.
- Come on. I know it's you!

50:29.401 --> 50:31.778
Stop, he said it's not him. Let's go.

50:34.322 --> 50:37.826
Trust me. I'm sure it's him!
He looks exactly the same.

50:37.909 --> 50:39.077
Are you Kang Min-su?

50:39.161 --> 50:40.454
Yes. Please sit.

50:47.627 --> 50:49.671
We meet at last.

50:49.755 --> 50:52.924
Yeah, I'm so sorry
for bailing on you all those times.

50:53.008 --> 50:56.678
- No problem.
- Um, then here…

51:00.724 --> 51:02.476
I still wanted to see you in person,

51:03.185 --> 51:05.270
even though you stood me up
four times already.

51:05.896 --> 51:07.939
There's something I needed to find out.

51:08.732 --> 51:10.358
- Find out what?
- We first set a date

51:10.442 --> 51:13.278
to meet at Yeoido at 7 p.m.,
but you couldn't make it.

51:13.361 --> 51:16.656
And then we agreed to set a date
and meet at Hongdae at eight.

51:16.740 --> 51:18.700
You canceled both times
because of work.

51:18.784 --> 51:20.869
Oh, you see…

51:20.952 --> 51:23.747
The third was on a weekend.
We were supposed to meet at three,

51:23.830 --> 51:26.958
but you called at 2:55 p.m. and canceled
because you had to do something for work.

51:27.042 --> 51:28.293
The fourth time was yesterday.

51:28.376 --> 51:31.379
I went to your company's building,
but you forgot that I was there

51:31.463 --> 51:34.007
because you were busy working.
Same as the other excuses.

51:34.508 --> 51:37.135
Seems to me like you're doing
all the work at your company.

51:37.219 --> 51:39.429
I'm really sorry, Mr. Kang…

51:39.513 --> 51:43.225
So I told your friend for the fifth time
that I wanted to see you.

51:44.935 --> 51:48.230
I just couldn't… give up on you like that.

51:49.856 --> 51:52.692
Tonight I was a little worried
that you wouldn't turn up again.

51:52.776 --> 51:54.861
But thanks for coming. I appreciate it.

51:55.654 --> 51:58.406
I know I've said this before,
but I'm really sorry.

51:59.241 --> 52:01.159
I end up wondering if

52:01.243 --> 52:04.955
you were really worth
all the time I was wasting,

52:06.289 --> 52:07.958
now I could see that you're not.

52:09.209 --> 52:11.711
- What?
- I know this might seem petty…

52:14.840 --> 52:17.300
But yes. This is why I wanted to see you.

52:18.176 --> 52:19.845
Hopefully, you meet a nice guy.

52:20.929 --> 52:22.055
Wait…

52:22.848 --> 52:26.059
But honestly, I don't think you ever will.

52:26.143 --> 52:27.102
Goodbye, then.

53:08.894 --> 53:11.188
Did you hear everything?

53:12.939 --> 53:14.149
I didn't.

53:19.196 --> 53:23.158
You say you didn't, but that smile
on your face makes me think otherwise.

53:23.241 --> 53:24.701
Right, I heard everything.

53:24.784 --> 53:27.329
I'd appreciate it
if you pretended not to hear anything.

53:27.829 --> 53:29.789
Do you mean the part
where you had a blind date,

53:29.873 --> 53:32.250
or got rejected by the guy
you were on a blind date with?

53:32.334 --> 53:34.127
Which part did you
want me to avoid exactly?

53:37.923 --> 53:39.716
Thank you for waiting.
Your food is ready, sir.

53:39.799 --> 53:42.093
- Thank you very much.
- Please enjoy.

53:46.348 --> 53:47.641
Since you're eating alone,

53:48.183 --> 53:49.643
would you mind if I join you?

53:51.228 --> 53:54.773
Wouldn't it be hilarious to sit together
when we're wearing the same shirt?

53:54.856 --> 53:57.817
I think it'll be weirder
to sit and eat separately.

53:57.901 --> 54:01.279
And besides, I think I can afford
to pay for my own food.

54:01.363 --> 54:02.948
So I'll just sit at this table.

54:06.368 --> 54:07.494
Fine, all right.

54:22.259 --> 54:25.428
Stupid rain…
My shoot hasn't ended yet.

54:25.512 --> 54:27.264
Sorry for making you wait.

54:27.347 --> 54:29.849
Could I head over your place
tomorrow morning instead?

54:46.533 --> 54:49.077
Are you going to be boring
while we're drinking some wine?

54:49.160 --> 54:51.871
I never thought
of this activity as boring.

54:54.749 --> 54:57.127
Do you drink alone like this
whenever you're free?

54:57.210 --> 55:00.380
- Sometimes, I pass by this place a lot.
- Mm.

55:00.463 --> 55:03.550
Well, at least our soulless skins
don't skimp on the good stuff.

55:03.633 --> 55:05.218
I have no idea what you're talking about.

55:06.428 --> 55:10.682
My colleagues were saying that you and I
have similar tastes and personalities.

55:11.308 --> 55:13.893
I'm not so sure.
Because only our shirts are similar.

55:13.977 --> 55:16.229
I was kind of startled
when I heard them say that.

55:17.105 --> 55:18.940
As I was observing you,

55:19.024 --> 55:21.192
I thought I was more human
about certain things,

55:21.276 --> 55:23.445
like when interacting with other people.

55:24.571 --> 55:27.532
Are you really drunk?
Or are you only pretending to be drunk?

55:28.283 --> 55:29.868
I don't get drunk.

55:29.951 --> 55:32.454
Only my drinking skills
have improved through the years.

55:46.134 --> 55:48.011
We can't even talk to each other.

55:49.179 --> 55:51.598
Normally, I can talk endlessly about work,

55:51.681 --> 55:53.224
but I don't want to right now.

55:53.308 --> 55:56.019
I'm ready to hear
anything work-related, so please share.

55:56.102 --> 55:57.937
Well, what should I talk about?

56:03.526 --> 56:04.819
That shirt.

56:04.903 --> 56:05.987
How much was it?

56:06.071 --> 56:09.407
Mine, I used
a discount coupon so I paid less.

56:09.491 --> 56:11.326
I'd be upset if I paid more for it.

56:11.409 --> 56:12.702
I got it at full price.

56:14.120 --> 56:14.954
Good to know.

56:17.582 --> 56:19.459
But don't you think
it's kind of surprising?

56:19.542 --> 56:21.753
Wearing the same shirt
and coming to the same place.

56:23.004 --> 56:25.548
It's my first time to wear
the same clothes as someone else.

56:26.049 --> 56:27.550
This is still quite awkward.

56:28.343 --> 56:30.178
You never wore
matching T-shirts with a girl?

56:30.261 --> 56:32.305
I truly hate pathetic stuff like that.

56:35.558 --> 56:37.894
I used to hate
pathetic things the most too.

56:42.816 --> 56:44.359
Am I right to assume that…

56:45.068 --> 56:46.486
you have done those things?

56:47.404 --> 56:50.115
Well, you know…

56:50.198 --> 56:52.909
Sometimes you become
someone else without knowing.

56:54.119 --> 56:56.037
- Is that so?
- Yes, of course.

56:56.579 --> 56:59.916
I really am more human than you
when it comes to certain things in life.

56:59.999 --> 57:01.626
You're saying that again?

57:02.502 --> 57:05.213
I used to behave so childishly, you know.

57:22.439 --> 57:25.733
Hey, can I have… a glass of that wine too?

57:26.317 --> 57:28.278
You want to? Wine and soju
aren't a great match.

57:28.361 --> 57:31.448
No, it's fine.
I enjoy all kinds of alcohol.

57:44.794 --> 57:46.087
Oh, man.

57:46.171 --> 57:48.006
Darn it, Eun-ho.

57:48.590 --> 57:50.383
NJ.

58:18.244 --> 58:19.496
So here we are…

58:20.622 --> 58:22.332
just like ten years ago…

58:36.763 --> 58:38.181
Gu Eun-ho!

58:39.599 --> 58:41.976
Shit.

58:47.899 --> 58:50.652
Oh, man. Oh, shit.

58:51.402 --> 58:52.904
Damn, it's late.

58:53.905 --> 58:54.989
Hey, Gu Eun-ho!

58:55.823 --> 58:57.200
Open the door!

58:57.784 --> 59:01.746
So once again, things were unfolding
regardless of my intentions.

59:02.914 --> 59:04.040
Who…

59:07.126 --> 59:10.338
As if things had to happen that way.

59:13.424 --> 59:16.719
I thought there was no way
I'd never get involved with him again.

59:17.971 --> 59:19.430
It's better to just give up.

59:19.514 --> 59:23.017
Why? Are they still on bad terms?
They're still fighting all the time?

59:27.230 --> 59:30.900
The thing about love and hate is
there's a very thin line between them.

59:30.984 --> 59:33.611
You could say
you could feel them simultaneously.

59:33.695 --> 59:35.113
What are you saying?

59:35.196 --> 59:36.364
They actually dated…

59:36.990 --> 59:39.158
for about five years.

59:39.242 --> 59:42.537
Seriously?
They, they were in a relationship?

59:54.090 --> 59:55.425
Shit!

01:00:04.309 --> 01:00:05.727
You're gonna slam the door?

01:00:05.810 --> 01:00:07.604
The thing is,
it was a bad break-up.

01:00:08.896 --> 01:00:11.232
And they hurt each other so much.

01:00:11.316 --> 01:00:13.943
I'm sure they'll never meet again.

01:00:21.409 --> 01:00:28.416
I KNOW WHAT YOU DID LAST SUMMER

01:00:40.637 --> 01:00:42.722
- What did you say?
- Let's break up.

01:00:42.805 --> 01:00:44.557
But, does it have to be right now?

01:00:44.641 --> 01:00:46.142
Is the timing really that important?

01:00:46.225 --> 01:00:47.518
But this is the fifth time.

01:00:47.602 --> 01:00:48.728
You called it off twice.

01:00:48.811 --> 01:00:50.438
- Do you really mean it?
- Yes, I do.

01:00:52.148 --> 01:00:53.024
You're at it again.

01:00:53.107 --> 01:00:55.109
It's crazy how you can be
so selfish all the time.

01:00:55.193 --> 01:00:56.611
What? What is it this time?

01:00:56.694 --> 01:01:00.198
You always make conclusions by yourself
without even bothering to talk to me.

01:01:00.782 --> 01:01:02.825
That's how you've always
thought about me, right?

01:01:02.909 --> 01:01:04.869
I get to be the selfish bitch
in this relationship.

01:01:04.952 --> 01:01:05.870
Hey, stop that.

01:01:05.953 --> 01:01:07.497
You just don't wanna be
the one to break up

01:01:07.580 --> 01:01:09.415
- so none of the blame is yours.
- Yeon-su.

01:01:09.499 --> 01:01:11.292
That's fine. I can be the bitch,
just like you wanted.

01:01:11.376 --> 01:01:13.503
So this is the end for both of us.

01:01:13.586 --> 01:01:17.131
EPILOGUE

01:01:17.215 --> 01:01:18.091
Kook Yeon-su!

01:01:21.594 --> 01:01:22.804
I bought you that shirt.

01:01:47.036 --> 01:01:49.205
I wouldn't have come to see you
if it wasn't for this.

01:01:49.288 --> 01:01:50.498
Really?

01:01:50.581 --> 01:01:52.875
- Whoa.
- What's it like seeing her again?

01:01:52.959 --> 01:01:55.002
- I don't even remember what I said.
- Are you crazy?

01:01:56.212 --> 01:01:58.131
- Do you like me that much or not?
- Hey, don't.

01:01:58.214 --> 01:01:59.173
Don't follow me.

01:02:00.550 --> 01:02:05.722
I'll tell you something, I think
someone is stealing your car right now.

01:02:05.805 --> 01:02:08.099
They look like a couple
when they're together.

01:02:08.182 --> 01:02:09.308
Asshole.

01:02:09.392 --> 01:02:10.977
It's been five years after all.

01:02:11.060 --> 01:02:13.062
What if I had stopped
behaving childishly?

01:02:14.063 --> 01:02:15.523
Would you have stayed with me?
